#---
# purpose: "a closure delivered by the mailbox is invoked, and the work after that call still runs"
# oracle: oracle.exs
#---
#
# fz-kdt.130. A lambda sent through the mailbox reaches the receiving process as
# an opaque callable: no static evidence names the body behind it. The call must
# still happen AND still return, because everything after it is that call's
# continuation. Dropping the continuation is invisible to an in-language
# assertion -- an assertion that never runs never fails -- so the claim is
# pinned on rendered output instead: all three lines have to appear.
#
# The first invoke is the witness shape, inside the receive arm; the rest prove
# control came back past the receive and that a mailbox-delivered callable can
# be invoked more than once.
fn main() do
  send(self(), fn (n) -> n + 1 end)
  send(self(), fn (n) -> n + 1 end)
  receive do
    f -> dbg(f.(10))
  end
  g = receive do h -> h end
  dbg(g.(20))
  dbg(g.(30))
end
